 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Great. Questions that show you' thought about the interview and the guest are always the most interesting. Start with something that hooks their interest, like a quote or a big challenge. Sure. I remember my grandmother's apple pie. It was so good, it made me want to bake it myself. That's a great starting point. Totally normal. A few quick tumbles help. A short pause to gather your thoughts is okay. It' polite, and it gives you confidence. A clear email with the questions also gives the guest a touch of host power. You' welcome. A great interview is a back and forth that builds interest. Your guest is your host, so make it a friendly conversation.",
